## 3. System Design

### 3.1 High-Level Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph Client["Client Layer"]
        WEB["React + Tailwind SPA"]
        MOB["Mobile App (future)"]
    end

    subgraph Gateway["API Gateway / Reverse Proxy"]
        NGINX["Nginx / Traefik"]
        RL["Rate Limiter (redis)"]
    end

    subgraph App["Application Layer"]
        API["Express API Server<br/>(Stateless, Horizontally Scalable)"]
        WS["WebSocket Server<br/>(Socket.io / ws)"]
        WORKER["Background Worker<br/>(BullMQ)"]
    end

    subgraph Data["Data Layer"]
        PG["PostgreSQL<br/>(Primary)"]
        PG_R["PostgreSQL<br/>(Read Replica)"]
        REDIS["Redis<br/>(Cache + Sessions + Queues)"]
        S3["Object Storage<br/>(S3 / MinIO)"]
    end

    subgraph External["External Services"]
        RZ["Razorpay"]
        SMS["SMS Gateway<br/>(Twilio / MSG91)"]
        EMAIL["Email<br/>(SendGrid / SES)"]
        PUSH["Push Notifications<br/>(FCM / APNs)"]
    end

    WEB & MOB --> NGINX
    NGINX --> RL --> API
    NGINX --> WS
    API --> PG
    API --> PG_R
    API --> REDIS
    API --> S3
    API --> RZ
    API --> WORKER
    WORKER --> PG
    WORKER --> SMS & EMAIL & PUSH
    WS --> REDIS
```

### 3.2 Component Responsibilities

| Component | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| **Nginx / Traefik** | TLS termination, load balancing, static file serving, WebSocket upgrade |
| **Redis** | JWT blocklist, rate-limit counters, session store, BullMQ job queues, real-time pub/sub for WebSocket fan-out |
| **Express API** | Stateless REST handlers, input validation (Zod/Joi), RBAC middleware, Razorpay SDK calls |
| **WebSocket Server** | Real-time push for emergency broadcasts, visitor check-in notifications, payment confirmations |
| **BullMQ Workers** | Invoice generation cron, overdue reminders, QR expiry cleanup, notification dispatch, report generation |
| **PostgreSQL Primary** | All writes, transactional integrity |
| **PostgreSQL Read Replica** | Dashboards, analytics, report queries |
| **Object Storage** | QR code images, invoice PDFs, user avatars, vendor documents |

### 3.3 Authentication & Authorization Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant A as API Server
    participant R as Redis
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    C->>A: POST /auth/login {email, password}
    A->>DB: SELECT user WHERE email = ?
    A->>A: bcrypt.compare(password, hash)
    A->>A: Sign JWT (access 15m + refresh 7d)
    A->>R: Store refresh token (key = user:id:refresh)
    A-->>C: { accessToken, refreshToken }

    Note over C,A: Subsequent requests
    C->>A: GET /invoices (Authorization: Bearer <access>)
    A->>A: Verify JWT signature + expiry
    A->>R: Check blocklist (is token revoked?)
    A->>A: RBAC check (role ∈ allowed roles)
    A->>DB: Query data
    A-->>C: 200 { data }
```

### 3.4 Payment Flow (Razorpay Integration)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant A as API Server
    participant RZ as Razorpay
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant W as Worker

    C->>A: POST /payments/create-order {invoiceId}
    A->>DB: Validate invoice (status, amount, ownership)
    A->>RZ: razorpay.orders.create({amount, currency})
    RZ-->>A: {rz_order_id}
    A->>DB: INSERT razorpay_txns (rz_order_id)
    A->>DB: INSERT payments (status: initiated)
    A-->>C: {rz_order_id, amount, key_id}

    C->>RZ: Razorpay Checkout UI (client-side)
    RZ-->>C: {rz_payment_id, rz_signature}

    C->>A: POST /payments/verify {rz_order_id, rz_payment_id, rz_signature}
    A->>A: HMAC-SHA256 verify signature
    A->>DB: UPDATE payments SET status=captured
    A->>DB: UPDATE invoice SET status=paid
    A->>DB: UPDATE razorpay_txns (rz_payment_id, signature)
    A-->>C: 200 { success }

    Note over RZ,A: Async webhook (backup)
    RZ->>A: POST /payments/webhook (payment.captured)
    A->>A: Verify webhook signature
    A->>DB: Idempotent upsert (skip if already captured)
    A->>W: Enqueue receipt email + push notification
```

### 3.5 QR Visitor Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant R as Resident
    participant A as API Server
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant S as Security Guard

    R->>A: POST /visitors {name, phone, validFrom, validUntil}
    A->>DB: INSERT visitor_pass
    A->>A: Generate HMAC token (passId + secret + expiry)
    A->>DB: INSERT qr_codes (token, expires_at)
    A-->>R: {pass, qrCodeUrl}

    R->>R: Share QR via WhatsApp/SMS

    S->>A: POST /visitors/verify-qr {token}
    A->>DB: SELECT qr_code WHERE token = ?
    A->>A: Check: expired? scanned_count < max_scans? pass status?
    alt Valid
        A->>DB: UPDATE scanned_count++, pass status=checked_in
        A->>A: Push notification to host resident (WebSocket)
        A-->>S: 200 {visitor details, unit, host}
    else Invalid
        A-->>S: 403 {reason: "expired" | "already_used" | "cancelled"}
    end
```

### 3.6 Emergency Broadcast Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant R as Resident
    participant A as API Server
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant WS as WebSocket
    participant W as Worker

    R->>A: POST /emergencies {type: "fire", severity: "critical"}
    A->>DB: INSERT emergency_alert
    A->>WS: Broadcast to building channel (real-time)
    A->>W: Enqueue SMS + Push to all building residents
    A->>W: Enqueue notification to security + admin
    A-->>R: 201 {alertId}

    Note over A,W: Worker processes
    W->>W: Send SMS via Twilio
    W->>W: Send Push via FCM
    W->>DB: INSERT notifications (in_app)
```

