## 4. Edge Cases & Production Concerns

### 4.1 Authentication

| Edge Case | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Brute-force login | Rate limit 10 req/min on `/auth/login`; progressive delay; account lockout after 5 failures (unlock via email) |
| JWT stolen | Short-lived access tokens (15 min); refresh token rotation; Redis blocklist on logout; bind refresh token to device fingerprint |
| Concurrent sessions | Track active sessions per user; allow configurable max (e.g. 3); force logout oldest on overflow |
| Role escalation | Server-side RBAC middleware on every route; never trust client-supplied role; validate role transitions (admin can't self-promote to super_admin) |

### 4.2 Visitor & QR

| Edge Case | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| QR screenshot replay | `max_scans` limit (default 1); HMAC token includes expiry, validated server-side; `scanned_count` prevents re-use |
| Pass valid window crossed | Cron job marks expired passes; verify-qr checks `valid_until` AND `qr.expires_at` |
| Visitor never checks out | Auto-checkout cron after 12 hours; security dashboard highlights stale check-ins |
| Resident creates passes after moving out | `user_units.moved_out_at` check; deactivated users blocked via `is_active` flag |

### 4.3 Payments

| Edge Case | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Double payment | Idempotency key on `create-order`; unique constraint `(invoice_id, rz_order_id)`; webhook handler checks existing captured status before updating |
| Partial payment | `payments.amount` can be less than `invoices.amount`; invoice tracks total paid; status becomes `partially_paid` |
| Webhook arrives before client verify | Both paths are idempotent; whichever arrives first captures, second is a no-op |
| Razorpay downtime | Queue failed orders for retry (BullMQ); show "pending" UI; manual cash/cheque fallback with admin approval |
| Refund race condition | Refund only from `captured` status; database transaction with `SELECT FOR UPDATE` on payment row |
| Invoice generated for vacant unit | Validate `unit.status = 'occupied'` before invoice generation; skip vacant units in bulk generation |

### 4.4 Parking

| Edge Case | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Double assignment | Unique constraint on `(slot_id)` in active assignments (where `assigned_until IS NULL OR assigned_until > now()`) |
| Slot type mismatch | Validate `vehicle_type` against `slot_type` (bike → two_wheeler only) |
| Resident moves out but keeps slot | Trigger slot release on `user_units.moved_out_at` update; cron audit |

### 4.5 Vendor Services

| Edge Case | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Vendor no-show | Auto-escalate if status stays `assigned` > 24h; notify admin |
| Disputed service | `disputed` status triggers admin review; freeze vendor rating updates until resolved |
| Concurrent requests for same vendor | Queue-based assignment; vendor capacity tracking (max concurrent jobs) |
| Rating manipulation | One rating per completed request; rate only after `status = 'completed'` |

### 4.6 Emergency System

| Edge Case | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| False alarm spam | Rate limit: 1 emergency per user per 5 min; repeated false alarms → admin review flag |
| No security online | Escalation ladder: security (0 min) → admin (2 min) → emergency contacts (5 min) via SMS if unacknowledged |
| Mass panic (100+ simultaneous alerts) | Deduplicate by type + building within 5-min window; merge into single broadcast; queue SMS to prevent provider throttle |
| Network down during emergency | Client caches SOS locally; retries with exponential backoff; offline-first emergency contact display |

### 4.7 System-Wide

| Concern | Strategy |
|---|---|
| **Data consistency** | Database transactions (`BEGIN...COMMIT`) for multi-table writes; `SELECT FOR UPDATE` for contested resources |
| **Soft deletes** | `is_active` / `deleted_at` on user-facing entities; hard delete only in audit-log archival |
| **Multi-tenancy** | `complex_id` scoping on all queries; RLS (Row-Level Security) in PostgreSQL for defense-in-depth |
| **Horizontal scaling** | Stateless API servers behind load balancer; Redis for shared state; sticky sessions only for WebSocket |
| **Observability** | Structured JSON logging (Winston/Pino); request-id propagation; Prometheus metrics; health-check endpoint `/health` |
| **DB migrations** | Versioned migrations via `node-pg-migrate` or Knex; zero-downtime deploys with backward-compatible schema changes |
| **Secrets management** | Environment variables via `.env` (dev) / Vault / AWS SSM (prod); never commit secrets |
| **CORS & CSP** | Strict CORS whitelist; Content-Security-Policy headers; Helmet.js middleware |
| **File uploads** | Size limits (5 MB avatar, 10 MB docs); virus scan via ClamAV; signed URLs for private access |
| **Backup & DR** | Daily automated PG backups (pg_dump); point-in-time recovery; cross-region replica for DR |

---

> **Architect** — This schema supports thousands of units with sub-second query response times when combined with the indexed strategy above. The modular Express structure allows each module to be extracted into a microservice later if traffic demands it.
